From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:35:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0009: AJM job on a destroyed instance fails

A batch started before the game destroyed an AJM instance can reach the
worker after the destroy (FIFA 22, as a menu stops its sounds). The
assertion ended the emulator; the job now fails as an invalid parameter.
Upstream defect, still on main on 2026-10-27. (0008 was an upstream
change that main has since.)

Details: tools/shadps4/README.md in the GameFlex repository, entry 0009.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/libraries/ajm/ajm_context.cpp | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/libraries/ajm/ajm_context.cpp b/src/core/libraries/ajm/ajm_context.cpp
index 8ce8f343..1f2f81d3 100644
--- a/src/core/libraries/ajm/ajm_context.cpp
+++ b/src/core/libraries/ajm/ajm_context.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "core/libraries/ajm/ajm_instance.h"
 #include "core/libraries/ajm/ajm_instance_statistics.h"
 #include "core/libraries/ajm/ajm_mp3.h"
+#include "core/libraries/ajm/ajm_result.h"
 #include "core/libraries/error_codes.h"
 
 #include <span>
@@ -86,7 +87,17 @@ void AjmContext::ProcessBatch(u32 id, std::span<AjmJob> jobs) {
             {
                 std::shared_lock lock(instances_mutex);
                 auto* p_instance = instances.Get(job.instance_id & INSTANCE_ID_MASK);
-                ASSERT_MSG(p_instance != nullptr, "Attempting to execute job on null instance");
+                if (p_instance == nullptr) {
+                    // GameFlex: a batch started before the game destroyed this instance reaches
+                    // the worker after the destroy (FIFA 22, as a menu stops its sounds). The
+                    // assertion ended the emulator; the job fails instead, as a bad parameter.
+                    LOG_WARNING(Lib_Ajm, "Job of batch {} for destroyed instance {}", id,
+                                job.instance_id);
+                    if (job.output.p_result) {
+                        job.output.p_result->result = ORBIS_AJM_RESULT_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+                    }
+                    continue;
+                }
                 instance = *p_instance;
             }
 
